[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was filed as one issue with one fix. It held three problems. The desk
merged every report whose subject line matched ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)),
and three problems share those subjects. Each has its own ticket.

Engineering closed #4471 on 5 October: the parser is fixed (`fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`)
and the `booking-v3` form is retired, so its hint won't be fixed.

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 is closed, and one problem in it is not fixed. Dates that move by one day are still open: neither
the parser fix nor retiring the form reaches them.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {tickets} />

Each report is counted once (the export repeats some), by its tenant's locale and booking form, never by
intake's tag: the tag is a guess from the reporter's browser.

## The three problems

**`parser` — the shared parser reads dates month first.** Every tenant here writes the day first, so a
date with a day of 12 or less swaps: 7 April goes out as 4 July. Covers app and email reports from every
tenant, and form reports from `booking-v2`. Fixed.

**`hint` — the `booking-v3` form asks for `MM/DD/YYYY`.** Clients of day-first tenants type what the
hint says, and the form reads it day first. The result looks like the parser bug and has a different fix:
the hint. The #4471 page already placed these apart ("no ticket of its own"); now they have one.
Won't fix: the form is retired, so no new reports of this kind can come in.

**`one-day` — dates move by one day.** Not a swap: Tuesday 12 May shows as Monday 11 May; a Lisbon
client gets Tuesday and a Toronto client Monday for the same meeting; an invite arrives before the booking
was made. That points at time zones. The desk had already noted these as a one-day move; the #4471
page counts them under `parser`, where the parser fix doesn't reach them. Still open. One reporter has
stopped reporting it, so expect more than the export shows.

## For triage

- A matching subject is not a matching cause. Before you merge into a big ticket, check the
  [cause explorer](/kb/triage/dedupe) for the tenant and channel.
- A date that moves by one day is never the parser. File it under the `one-day` ticket.

